# Netlify

- Build: **`pnpm run build`** (see `netlify.toml`). Set **Node 22** via `NODE_VERSION` if not inherited from the file.
- Required site env vars: **`DATABASE_URL`**, **`BETTER_AUTH_SECRET`**, **`BETTER_AUTH_URL`**, **`NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL`** (production URL must match Better Auth `baseURL` / trusted origins).
- Payments: **`PAYMENT_PROVIDER`** (`paddle` default \| `ziina`). Ziina needs **`ZIINA_ACCESS_TOKEN`**, **`ZIINA_WEBHOOK_SECRET`** (required in prod for `/api/webhooks/ziina`), optional **`ZIINA_API_BASE_URL`**, **`ZIINA_TEST_MODE`**, **`ZIINA_ENFORCE_WEBHOOK_IP_ALLOWLIST`**. See `docs/superpowers/specs/2026-04-24-payment-provider-env-switch-design.md` §16.
- Fincra (per-checkout NGN for Nigerian nationality, flag off by default): **`FINCRA_ENABLED`**, **`FINCRA_API_BASE_URL`** (`https://sandboxapi.fincra.com` / `https://api.fincra.com`), **`FINCRA_SECRET_KEY`**, **`FINCRA_PUBLIC_KEY`**, **`FINCRA_BUSINESS_ID`**, **`FINCRA_WEBHOOK_SECRET`**, optional **`FINCRA_FEE_BEARER`** (`business` default \| `customer`). Webhook: `POST /api/webhooks/fincra`. Runtime only (not `NEXT_PUBLIC_*`). Fincra IP-allowlists the portal server; sandbox calls from other VMs will fail.
- Run **`pnpm run db:migrate`** (or apply SQL from `drizzle/`) against the Neon branch used by that deploy context before relying on auth.
